.TH ZONAR 8
.SH NAME
zonar \- Show file system use of zoned devices

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zonar
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...] \fIpath\fP
.br
.B zonar
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...] \fB\-\-connect\fR \fIipaddr\fP
.br
.B zonar
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...] \fB\-\-listen\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zonar
provides a graphical interface to visualize blockgroups of a zoned
filesystem. \fBzonar\fP also allows inspecting the file extents
stored in blockgroups as well as the location on the device of file extents.
When not using the \fR\-\-connect\fP or \fR\-\-listen\fP options, \fIpath\fP
must specify the mount directory of the file system to inspect.

Currently \fBzonar\fP supports the XFS and btrfs file systems.

.SS Local mode
When \fIpath\fP is specified, \fBzonar\fP inspects a local file system and
should be run as a regular user. Accessing the device information requires
root privileges, so \fBzonar\fP starts the server
\fBzonar_srv\fP(8) as a child process using \fBpkexec\fP(1), which prompts
for administrator authentication. Only the server runs with root privileges.
The graphical interface communicates with the server in reverse connection
mode on the loopback address, and the server is stopped when \fBzonar\fP exits.

When the polkit action file installed with \fBzonar\fP is used, authentication
is only allowed from an active local session. Inactive and remote sessions are
denied.

.SS Remote mode
With the \fR\-\-connect\fP or \fR\-\-listen\fP options, \fBzonar\fP inspects
a file system on a remote system running \fBzonar_srv\fP(8).

.SH OPTIONS
\fBzonar\fP options are as follows.
.TP
.BR \-\-help,\ \-h
Display a command line help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose,\ \-v
Enable verbose mode (for debugging).
.TP
.BR \-\-version,\ \-V
Display \fBzonar\fP version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-connect,\ \-c\ \fIipaddr\fP
Specify the IP address of the server to connect to. This option cannot be used
together with the option \fR\-\-listen\fP. If used, a mount directory
\fIpath\fP must not be specified.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen,\ \-l
Reverse connection mode: instead of connecting to the server, listen for
connections from the server.  This option cannot be used together with the
option \fR\-\-connect\fP. If used, a mount directory \fIpath\fP must not be
specified.
.TP
.BR \-\-port,\ \-p\ \fIport\fP
Specify the port number to connect to the server or to listen for connection
on. The default port is 49152.
.TP
.BR \-\-server,\ \-s\ \fIpath\fP
Local mode only: run the server binary specified by \fIpath\fP instead of the
installed \fBzonar_srv\fP. This is intended for development, for example to
run a server binary from a build directory that is not installed. The polkit
action installed with \fBzonar\fP only applies to the installed
\fBzonar_srv\fP, so \fBpkexec\fP default authentication rules apply when this
option is used.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.wdc.zonar.policy
polkit action file defining the \fIorg.wdc.zonar.srv\fP action used to run
\fBzonar_srv\fP in local mode. The installation directory can be changed with
the \fR\-\-with\-polkit\-actiondir\fP configure option.

